A classifier closer to the upper-left corner achieves a high true positive rate with a low false positive rate.

## Area under the ROC curve

The ROC AUC summarizes the ROC curve as a single number:

- 1.0 represents perfect discrimination;
- 0.5 corresponds to random ranking;
- values below 0.5 indicate rankings worse than random.

::: {#roc-auc-sgd .cell execution_count=33}
